  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the oven to 375°F (190°C).",
    "In a large mixing bowl, combine the spinach, parsley, scallions, feta cheese, ground almonds, cottage cheese, egg, jalapeno pepper, beurre-monte, flour, salt, and black pepper. Mix well to combine.",
    "Roll out the phyllo dough to a thickness of about 1/8 inch. Cut it into a rectangle that is slightly larger than the tart pan or pie dish.",
    "Brush the bottom of the tart pan or pie dish with some of the melted butter. Place a sheet of phyllo dough in the pan, brushing it with some of the melted butter. Repeat this process 5-6 times, until all of the phyllo dough is used.",
    "Pour the spinach mixture into the phyllo-lined pan, spreading it evenly to the edges. Dot the top of the spinach mixture with some of the melted butter.",
    "Fold the edges of the phyllo dough over the filling, pressing gently to seal. Brush the top of the pie with some of the melted butter.",
    "Bake the pie for about 35-40 minutes, or until the phyllo dough is golden brown and the filling is hot and bubbly.",
    "Remove the pie from the oven and let it cool for a few minutes. Serve warm, garnished with some additional parsley and lemon zest, if desired."
  ],
